("p", "**Example.** 2x + 3y = 7 and (k &minus; 1)x + (k + 2)y = 3k have infinitely many solutions. Then 2/(k &minus; 1) = 3/(k + 2), so 2k + 4 = 3k &minus; 3 and **k = 7**; check 7/(3k) = 7/21 = 1/3, which equals 2/6. **Example:** kx + 3y = 3 and 12x + ky = 6 have no solution if k/12 = 3/k &ne; 1/2: k<sup>2</sup> = 36, k = 6 or &minus;6, and k/12 &ne; 1/2 rules out 6, so **k = &minus;6**."),
